---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy — BlackWhitePDF";
const description =
  "Privacy Policy for BlackWhitePDF. Learn how our grayscale and black and white PDF converter processes files in your browser and what information we collect.";
const path = "/privacy/";
const updated = "August 8, 2026";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: title,
  description,
  url: new URL(path, Astro.site ?? "https://blackwhitepdf.com").href,
  dateModified: "2026-08-08",
  isPartOf: {
    "@type": "WebSite",
    name: "BlackWhitePDF",
    url: new URL("/", Astro.site ?? "https://blackwhitepdf.com").href,
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  current="privacy"
  keywords="blackwhitepdf privacy policy, private pdf converter, grayscale pdf privacy"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <main id="main" class="scroll-mt-4 border-b border-hairline bg-canvas">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
      <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-mute">Legal</p>
      <h1
        class="text-[34px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-1.4px] text-balance md:text-[40px] md:tracking-[-1.8px]"
      >
        Privacy Policy.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mute">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
        This Privacy Policy explains how BlackWhitePDF (“we”, “us”, or “our”) handles
        information when you use our website and grayscale / black and white PDF converter
        at this domain (the “Service”).
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">1. Summary</h2>
        <p>
          PDF conversion runs entirely in your browser. We do not upload, store, or process
          the contents of your PDF files on our servers as part of the conversion feature.
          Your documents stay on your device during rendering, filtering, and download.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">2. Information we process</h2>
        <h3 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">2.1 PDF files you convert</h3>
        <p>
          When you select a PDF, the file is read locally by your browser. Conversion,
          cropping, and export happen client-side. We do not receive a copy of that PDF
          for processing. If you close the page before downloading, the working copy in
          memory is discarded by your browser.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">2.2 Technical and usage data</h3>
        <p>
          Like most websites, our hosting or analytics providers (if enabled) may collect
          standard technical data such as IP address, browser type, device type, referring
          URL, pages visited, and approximate location derived from IP. This data is used
          to operate, secure, and improve the Service. We do not use your PDF contents for
          advertising.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">2.3 Cookies and similar technologies</h3>
        <p>
          We may use essential cookies or local storage required for site operation. If we
          use optional analytics cookies, you can control them through your browser
          settings. Clearing site data removes locally stored preferences where applicable.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">3. How we use information</h2>
        <p>We use non-document technical data to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Deliver and maintain the website and converter.</li>
          <li>Monitor performance, abuse, and security issues.</li>
          <li>Understand aggregate traffic so we can improve SEO content and features.</li>
          <li>Comply with legal obligations when required.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">4. Sharing of information</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell your personal information. We may share limited technical data with
          infrastructure providers (for example hosting, CDN, or analytics) who process it
          on our behalf under appropriate agreements. We may disclose information if required
          by law, to protect rights and safety, or in connection with a merger or asset
          transfer of the Service.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">5. Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          Converted PDFs are not retained by us because they are not uploaded for conversion.
          Technical logs and analytics data, if collected, are retained only as long as needed
          for the purposes above or as required by law.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">6. Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable measures to protect the website. Because conversion is local,
          your primary risk surface is your own device and browser. Keep your software
          updated and avoid converting highly sensitive files on shared or untrusted
          computers.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">7. International visitors</h2>
        <p>
          The Service may be hosted or delivered through infrastructure in multiple regions.
          By using the website you understand that technical data may be processed in
          countries other than your own, subject to applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">8. Children’s privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is not directed to children under 13 (or the equivalent minimum age
          in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect personal information from
          children.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">9. Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop using the Service at any time. You can block cookies in your browser.
          Because PDFs are processed locally, there is no document account to delete for
          conversion history.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">10. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at
          the top will change when we do. Continued use of the Service after changes means
          you accept the revised policy.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] text-ink">11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this Privacy Policy? Reach out through our
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-link underline hover:text-link-deep">Contact</a> page,
          or learn more about us on the
          <a href="/about/" class="text-link underline hover:text-link-deep">About Us</a> page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
